	"$comment": "The public surface the vendored WOO bundle (build/woo, served by BundledSiteController at /woo) draws, authored as Portaliq content (openspec/changes/retire-the-vendored-woo-bundle, task 2). Home, themes, search, one publication and the GEMMA page are page rows built only from blocks the public site renders; the navigation is a menu row, so an editor changes it without a deploy. Sign-in is the portal's own auth edge (DigiD, eHerkenning), never a bundled screen. A municipality installs it with `occ portaliq:example-site:install open-publicaties` and then sets its own domain, theme and organisation on the portal row. Nothing here names a real organisation.",
